  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool) is the current best at 0.591 acc, and the only RNA encoder tested so far is PCA. We have zero data on whether a learned encoder (scvi, scgpt) can improve upon PCA. Image-only is very weak (0.208), so the RNA branch dominates performance. Uncertainty: The RNA encoder choice is a fundamental design decision that propagates to all multimodal configurations, yet it is completely untested. What this tests: config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) is a clean A/B comparison against config_002—identical profile setting and aggregation, only the encoder changes. This isolates the effect of a learned variational encoder vs. linear PCA. Why best next: If scvi significantly outperforms PCA, it reshapes the entire search (prioritize scvi in multimodal); if it is comparable, PCA is sufficient and we can pivot to fusion strategy. Either outcome reduces the largest remaining uncertainty and directly informs the next 3-4 experiments, making it the highest-information-per-experiment choice under a limited budget."
}

